Input: add driver for the Awinic AW8697 LRA haptic controller

The Xiaomi 12 (cupid) and its SM8450 siblings drive their vibration motor
with an Awinic AW8697 on I2C. Mainline has no driver for it (aw86927.c,
added in 6.17, is a different register map).

This is a small mainline-style driver written from Xiaomi's downstream
driver (drivers/input/misc/aw8697_haptic in MiCode zeus-s-oss) and the
cupid downstream devicetree:

- regmap over I2C, reset GPIO, chip id 0x97, soft reset;
- the downstream init sequence: 24 kHz PWM, boost and LRA tuning,
  motor protection off, offset calibration, hardware vbat compensation;
- open-loop f0 detection at probe and the LRA oscillator trim derived
  from it, as downstream does on every boot;
- the waveform library (aw8697_haptic.bin from the vendor firmware) is
  written into the chip SRAM asynchronously after probe;
- a memoryless FF_RUMBLE input device. A rumble loops waveform 11
  (downstream's timed-vibration waveform) in RAM mode with the boost
  bypassed; the magnitude maps onto the digital gain 0x1e..0x80 with
  the same battery-voltage compensation downstream applies.

RTP streaming, the FIFO interrupt, the trigger inputs and the sysfs
tuning knobs of the downstream driver are left out.

